// /Hints/Stamps/Device: SSH capture

// This stamp will invoke a command on a remote system/device using SSH,
// and return the results in $Text. The start time will be stored in
// $StartDate, and execution elapsed time will be placed in $MyInterval.
// 
// The Stamped note should have these two Attribute assignments:
//   $SSH_Target: A string that provides either an IP address or a domain
//     name for the target system/device. This will be used as the
//     destination for the SSH command. Note that use of SSH keys is 
//     strongly recommended, though a userid and password could be 
//     passed directly via this attribute if security is not a concern.
//   $MyString: The actual command to be invoked by the remote system/device.
//     
$StartDate = date(now);
$Text += "ssh " + $SSH_Target + " '" + $MyString+"'\n";
$Text += (runCommand("ssh " + $SSH_Target + " '" + $MyString+"'"));
$MyInterval = interval($StartDate-date(now));


